    description: "[REVIEW 2026-11-01, CURRENT] 2026-11-01 review (dev 100b6fbb6e): survey of sherpa-onnx c-api emits no OfflineRecognizer class or methods from cxx-api.h; the 3 src_stands_in_for edges are exactly as filed (L126 MoveOnly, L159 if, L807 LinearResampler). Addition: the misparse also mints 15 one-line phantom classes named SHERPA_ONNX_API (e.g. cxx-api.h:392-392:SHERPA_ONNX_API:class). (Original text below; the review entry in the thread has the evidence.)\n\nFOUND 2026-10-01 (WI-tikop's description) and re-checked 2026-10-04 on branch jgstern-agent/fix/darik. class SHERPA_ONNX_API X : public MoveOnly<X, Y> { ... } -- an export macro tree-sitter-cpp cannot expand between class and the name -- parses as a function_definition whose declarator is the template MoveOnly<..> with an ERROR node for \"X : public\"; the class body becomes a compound_statement, so the class and EVERY method in it get no symbol (sherpa-onnx/c-api/cxx-api.h).\n\nWI-tikop's branch draws calls inside such a definition from the file and marks them src_stands_in_for, rather than dropping them. On sherpa-onnx that is 3 edges, and all 3 are misparse artifacts, not calls: \"if (p_ == nullptr)\" read as a call to if (cxx-api.h:159), \"LinearResampler() = default;\" (807) and \"MoveOnly() = default;\" (126). The marker says the src stands in; it cannot say the call itself is a parse artifact.\n\nThe cure is the parse, not a name: strip or tolerate the argument-less export macro before the class name (cf. WI-gafip for objc's attribute macros), after which the class and its methods are ordinary symbols. Not measured beyond sherpa-onnx (the measured C++ repos x265, falco, bento4, modsecurity had 0 such definitions)."  # 1aca
